    "created_at": "2025-08-29T17:33:46Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-08-29T17:33:46Z",
    "body": ">  other implementers for this kind of event.\n\nBlink does this lazily via a [dirty bit](https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/blink/renderer/core/html/forms/html_form_element.h;l=238;drc=5eb0af01e72f8733241dd5597c7926db3c6ee24a). Having said that, I don't see the harm of adding an event, if there's developer interest. Provided the event is asynchronous and coalesced. E.g. only one event fired if multiple elements change within one cycle of the event loop.\n\n",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
